    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17885" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτό-πρεμνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>together with the root,
				root and branch,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δ᾽ ἀντιτείνοντ᾽ αὐτόπρεμν᾽
			ἀπόλλυται</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δένδρα</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				714
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				231.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνασπᾶν αὐτοπρέμνοις τοῖς λόγοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					903
				</span></i>
			 (paratrag.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐ. τι νέμειν</span>
			give <i>in absolute possession,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				401
			</span></i>.</div>
